[26.876429, "o", "   - The filter should be a single string containing the complete jq filter expression\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[26.87682, "o", "**Note on examples below**: In the following Data Schema sections, all content following the '\"'\"'#'\"'\"' symbol is just explanatory commentary and will NOT appear in the actual JSON files. These comments are only provided to clarify the structure and requirements.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[26.876882, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[26.87692, "o", "**Input Data Schema**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[26.877034, "o", "The input JSON file '\"'\"'/app/users.json'\"'\"' is an array of user objects with the following structure:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[26.877044, "o", "> [\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[26.877081, "o", "\u001b[?2004h>   {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[26.87712, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[26.877194, "o", "    \"id\": 1,                  # Unique numeric identifier for the user\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[26.877222, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[26.877304, "o", "    \"username\": \"john_doe\",   # User'\"'\"'s unique username (string)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[26.877319, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[26.877337, "o", "> "]
[26.87743, "o", "    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",  # User'\"'\"'s email address (string)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[26.877449, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[26.877573, "o", "    \"status\": \"active\",       # User status: '\"'\"'active'\"'\"' or '\"'\"'inactive'\"'\"'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[26.877586, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[26.877611, "o", "> "]
[26.877743, "o", "    \"last_login\": \"2024-10-02T20:59:10.109812Z\",  # ISO 8601 timestamp (UTC) of the last login\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[26.87787, "o", "    \"roles\": [\"admin\", \"editor\"]  # Array of roles assigned to the user (may be empty)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[26.877932, "o", ">   },\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   ...\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[26.877999, "o", "]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[26.878101, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> **Output Data Schema**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[26.878147, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[26.878238, "o", "The output JSON file '\"'\"'/app/active_users_report.json'\"'\"' must be an array of objects with the following structure:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> [\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   {\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[26.87831, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[26.878374, "o", "    \"user_id\": 1,                 # Derived from '\"'\"'id'\"'\"' in input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[26.878459, "o", "    \"username\": \"john_doe\",       # Retained from input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[26.878474, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[26.878557, "o", "    \"email\": \"john@example.com\",  # Retained from input \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[26.878595, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[26.878685, "o", "    \"last_login\": \"2024-10-02\",   # Formatted from '\"'\"'last_login'\"'\"' in input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[26.878727, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[26.87881, "o", "    \"role_count\": 2,              # Count of '\"'\"'roles'\"'\"' from input\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
